    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CHiDwgQt3zHhvwRCXabv3x)_\n\n**Before:** the macOS section of the top-level `README.org` (added in #35) held the stack, the rules and a 14-row table of alternatives, which made it long.\n\n**After:** a new `adr/` folder at the repo root with an index (`adr/README.org`) and eight records about the AI workflow, one file each: plain clone for GUI tools (0001), SourceGit with the alternatives table (0002), merge commits on GitHub (0003), number-prefixed PR branches (0004), merging stacked PRs without rebasing (0005), `CHANGELOG.org` keep-both-sides (0006), Forge, code-review and the sandbox (0007), and `sp-vc-ai-workbench` as a brainstorming tool (0008). Each has context, decision, alternatives and consequences. The README section now has a short table of the current choices, each linked to its record, plus a short note on the workbench.\n\n`CHANGELOG.org`: adds the entry for this PR, and moves #35 (merged today) from Open pull requests to 2026-10-21.\n\n**Not verified:** same as #35. Written from a Linux container; nothing was run on the Mac, and untried tools are marked /untested/ in the records. The relative `file:` links were checked by reading, not by opening them in Emacs.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_015WpxMsqdEyLFUmgXrKUQvi)_",
